WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.934
-Josh, welcome back.
It is always great to see you.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:03.968
You know I love
when you come on.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.968
-It's good to be here.
-How's the kids?

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.133
How's the family?

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.434
-There's so many things
that they're into.

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.234
My daughter's 3 1/2,
my son's 7 1/2.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:13.701
So he's very much into Minecraft
and you know...

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.400
Pokémon, I'm sure, right?
I hear the moans.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.901
I hear the moans.
-You hear the -- Yeah.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:20.234
-No, and I was telling someone
the other day,

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.934
I was saying, you know,
some of the best acting

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.267
I've ever done in my life --

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.501
I mean, I'm talking
about Academy Award style --

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.334
-Yeah.
-...is pretending to my son

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.834
that I understand
what Pokémon is about.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.634
[ Laughter ]
No, I'm serious.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.634
Like, we have conversations
about it, and I'm like,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.968
"Really?"

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.367
"So that thing -- and how many
points is that one worth?

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.868
Oh, okay, cool."
By the way, I mean,

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.501
I can say this 'cause he's not
going to see the show --

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.167
I don't think he knows
what the hell it's about either.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:48.501
-No, no one knows about points.
I didn't know you get points.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.400
-His whole thing is always like,
"Oh, that's a fake card."

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.834
I'm like, "They're really in."

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.234
He's like, "No." I'm like,
"How can you tell it's a fake?"

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.934
He's like, "Dude, you rip it,

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:58.200
and, like, you can tell,
like, the paper."

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.834
I'm like, "I didn't buy you
a fake card.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.534
Where did you get
a fake card from?"

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:02.868
-I wanted you to come on,

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:04.601
I wanted you to bring
a Baltimore thing.

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:05.734
-Yeah.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.634
-Like a snack or something.
-Of course.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:08.968
-You brought me
something here tonight,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.868
which I'm very excited...
because I want to talk

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.033
about your new series,

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.167
but you brought me
a snowball maker.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:17.734
-Yes. This is why --
Well, you know, you were asking

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.167
to bring something
from Baltimore.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.000
And if I think about something
that is uniquely Baltimore,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.834
it's a snowball.
-Okay.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.367
-Similar to an Italian ice,
a little more granular.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.000
And, you know,
so I brought some...

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.400
This is my
Little Snowie machine.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.467
My Little Snowie Max.
-This is from your house?

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.501
-This is from my house.
My dad had one.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.000
And when I was in Baltimore,
I was like, I think I had like

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.434
six snowballs one night.
I was like,

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.234
"I think I need to get
one of these for my apartment."

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.167
So I have one.
-This was before you had kids?

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:46.167
-This is --
No, this is yesterday.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.667
And these are flavors
from a place in Baltimore

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.968
called Kavern Syrups,
and it's important.

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.000
The syrups are very important
because you can't have

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.501
any of that high-fructose
corn syrup crap.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.000
You know, these are
just pure 100% sugar

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.567
to pump into your --
to pump into your veins.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:06.567
-Okay. That quality sugar.
-Just 100% sugar.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.100
-But Kavern is the way to go
if you're going to get syrup.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.634
Kavern Syrups in Baltimore,
Maryland, is a great place.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:12.968
-Okay.
How do we do it?

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:15.067
-So, let me do it.
Let me make you some snowballs.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:16.300
-I appreciate this.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.734
-First, I'm gonna tell you,
this is very loud.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.667
So I don't know if the guys
want to, you know...

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.434
-No, they don't want to do...
-Well, I mean, you know.

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.467
-Let's talk about your -- I want
to talk about your show,

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.000
"We Own This City."
-Yeah.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.534
Well, it is based
in Baltimore, unlike...

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:31.801
[ Machine whirs ]

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.467
-What? What?!
-Yeah, well...

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:36.300
-[ Indistinct ]
-Where is it set?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.300
-Takes place in Baltimore!
-Set in Baltimore?!

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.801
-Yeah, it's great!
[ Whirring continues ]

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:41.133
[ Whirring stops ]
-Kids hear this sound,

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.300
they come running.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.400
Don't put your fingers
in there, Josh!

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.501
-Dude, you just gave kids
SpaghettiOs on a damn hot dog.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.234
Gonna worry about my fingers
in your snowball?

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.734
Get out of here, Fallon!

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:53.834
Alright.
-Okay.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:55.601
-Which flavor?
Now, here I have cherry.

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:58.234
I have Skylite, which was mine
as a kid growing up.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.234
And basically,
I just call it blue.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:02.267
I couldn't tell you what flavor.
-Blue is the flavor.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:05.367
-Spearmint for -- you know,
maybe for your parents.

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:08.234
And this is an egg custard,
right?

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.601
This is one of the...
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:12.133
Thank you.
This is one of the most unique,

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:14.100
original -- one of the first
flavors, I think.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.334
It was made originally with eggs
and vanilla and sugar and syrup.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:18.934
And this is a classic
Baltimore flavor.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.601
I would suggest you try this.
-Let's go with cherry.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.100
-Is that alright? Alright.
-Let's go with cherry.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:25.200
Let's start with cherry, then --
-You would pick cherry.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.934
-We'll work our way
to the egg custard!
-You would pick cherry.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.934
Really?
-Egg custard is what you want?!

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.734
-What do you want to go with?
-You want to have a hot dog off?

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.734
-Yeah, let's go, right now!
-Bring your egg custard

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:35.834
on the hot dog!
-Let's go!

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:37.300
Do you want cherry
or you want egg custard?

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.300
-Alright, give me egg custard.
Yeah.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.634
I'll make you one.

00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:42.300
-Alright, you make me one.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:49.200
♪♪

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.033
Ooh. Oh, I'm screwing it up.
There you go.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:53.734
-Oh, I see.
It's seeping right in there.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.234
-Yeah, you get it
all up in there.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.400
-Let me try this.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.100
-Alright, now. Here you go.
That's yours.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.667
-Bottoms up.
-What the hell did you do?

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.434
-It's like a mint julep.
Like a mint julep, like...

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:04.767
-Okay.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.300
That's the best.
That's the best.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.334
-That's what I'm telling you.
-That is the best.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.868
It's like a cream soda.
I love it.

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.467
-Give me the damn thing.
-Alright.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:18.000
Um, Josh...

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.801
Tell me about your show, please.

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.400
Who do you play?
This is a true story.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.901
-It's based on a true story.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:26.467
Justin Fenton, an incredible
reporter in Baltimore,

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:27.601
used to be
with The Baltimore Sun.

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.901
Now he's with
the Baltimore Banner.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.734
I had followed his reporting
very closely.

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.667
It's a true story about
the Gun Trace Task Force

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.501
and corruption
in Baltimore Police Department.

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.667
And David Simon
and George Pelecanos,

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.834
you know, created "The Wire."
-"The Wire," not too shabby.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.434
-This is their world,
and they know it well.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.434
[ Applause ]
Yes. Thank you.

00:04:44.434 --> 00:04:48.767
And, you know,
unlike a snowball,

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:51.601
it's not the most pleasant story
about Baltimore,

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.834
but one that's important
to be told.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:57.067
And yeah, it's all real,
and it really happened.

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.634
-I always love when you come on,
and congrats,

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.734
you're fantastic in this.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.701
Here's Josh Charles
in "We Own This City."

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.200
Take a look.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.367
-I could use your insight.
-Yeah? About what?

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:11.868
-Well, you have an impressive
number of complaints with IAD.

00:05:11.868 --> 00:05:13.501
46, by my count.

00:05:13.501 --> 00:05:15.934
-Only one sustained.
-But given the number --

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.234
-Ma'am.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.400
You know what the Baltimore cops
who don't have complaints

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.400
are doing every day?

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.467
-No.

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.100
-They sure as hell
ain't policing.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.167
-Mm.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:27.667
-'Cause if you want
to do this job,

00:05:27.667 --> 00:05:30.467
then you're gonna get complaints
for doing this job.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.667
-So what you're saying --
-I'm saying the reason

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.534
so many complaints
are unsustained

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.968
is 'cause they're coming
from criminals

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:39.300
who are being policed
for doing crime.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.267
And that's all I have to say.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.067
-Oh! Josh Charles!

00:05:43.067 --> 00:05:45.400
Check out the finale
of "We Own This City"

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.133
Monday on HBO.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:48.133
We love you, Josh Charles.

